So, the general formula for permutations when selecting r items from n without repetition is P(n, r) = n! / (n - r)!. Let me confirm that. Yes, that's right. So in this case, n is 20 members, and r is 3 positions (president, vice-president, treasurer). Therefore, the number of ways should be 20P3, which is 20! divided by (20 - 3)! which is 17!.

