Now, to convert seconds into minutes, I know that 1 minute is 60 seconds. So, I need to divide the total seconds by 60 to get the number of minutes. That would be 600 seconds divided by 60. Let me do that calculation. 600 divided by 60 is 10. So, 10 minutes.

Wait, let me double-check. If each dimple takes 2 seconds, then 300 dimples would take 300 * 2 = 600 seconds. Then, converting seconds to minutes: 600 / 60 = 10. Yeah, that seems right. So the answer should be 10 minutes.

