We can express 117 and 119 as 117 = 13 × 9 and 119 = 17 × 7. 

Therefore, 117 × 119 = (13 × 9) × (17 × 7) = 13 × 9 × 17 × 7.

Now, 9 is not a prime number. It can be factored further as 3 × 3. 

So, substituting back, 117 × 119 = 13 × 3 × 3 × 17 × 7.

Thus, the prime factors are 3, 7, 13, and 17. 

These are all distinct prime numbers. 

So, the number of different prime factors is 4.

