Make sure that the final matrix is a 2 × 2 matrix.

To find the projection matrix onto the y-axis, we need to consider the vector along the y-axis, which is $ \vec{v} = \begin{bmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix} $. 

Let's compute the norm squared of this vector. $ ||\vec{v}||^2 = 0^2 + 1^2 = 1 $.

Now, using the projection formula: $ \frac{1}{||\vec{v}||^2} \vec{v} \vec{v}^\top $. This becomes $ \frac{1}{1} \begin{bmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix} \begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix} $.

Multiplying these two matrices, we have:

$$
\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix} \begin{bmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} 0 \times 0 & 0 \times 1 \\ 1 \times 0 & 1 \times 1 \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix}
$$

So, the projection matrix onto the y-axis is $\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix}$.

