The exact value of the given sum is:

$$
\sum_{k=2}^{n} \frac{1}{k^2} = \left( \sum_{k=1}^{n} \frac{1}{k^2} \right) - 1
$$

So, the answer is:

$$
\boxed{ \left( \sum_{k=1}^{n} \frac{1}{k^2} \right) - 1 }
$$

